.TH TILAWAH 1 "September 2026" "tilawah 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tilawah \- terminal-native Qur'an audio player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tilawah
.RI [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.br
.B tilawah
.RI "play -r " NAME " -s " N
.br
.B tilawah
.RI "download -r " NAME " [-s " N " | --all]"
.br
.B tilawah
.RI "setup " URL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tilawah streams and offline-plays Qur'an audio from mp3quran.net (240+
reciters, Top-15 menu), keeps a personal shelf downloaded from a YouTube
playlist, and runs entirely in the terminal with an Islamic-geometric ambient
visual. One binary, no daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (no command)
Launch the TUI.
.TP
.B play -r NAME -s N
Play without the TUI.
.TP
.B download -r NAME [-s N | --surahs A B | --all]
Download audio for offline use (resumable, skips cached files).
.TP
.B get-playlist URL / setup URL
Download the personal YouTube shelf (needs yt-dlp); setup also remembers URL.
.TP
.B reciters [query] / surahs [query] / favs / history / shelf / resume
Browse the library, favorites, history and shelf from the shell.
.TP
.B shrink-shelf --bitrate 96k
Re-encode shelf audio to save space (duration-verified, needs ffmpeg).
.TP
.B theme NAME / doctor
Switch theme (night/dawn/minimal); check dependencies and connectivity.
.SH KEYS (TUI)
Space play/pause, n/p next/prev, 0 restart, Left/Right seek, Up/Down volume,
m mute, Tab panels, Enter play, / find, C all reciters, w narration,
f favorite, d save surah, a save reciter, t sleep timer, g theme,
v fullscreen, o move box, A animation, ? help, q quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tilawah/config.toml
Configuration (default reciter, theme, download dir, playlist URL, ...).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tilawah/tilawah.db
Catalog cache, history, favorites, positions, shelf (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/Tilawah/
Downloaded audio (overridable via config).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Project README and DECISIONS.md in /usr/share/doc/tilawah/.
